    "attachments" : [ {
      "content" : "A circuit that allows the user to play their own .ROM files using an unmodified Gameboy This circuit enables the user to play their own .ROM files using an actual Gameboy - no more software emulators! The user-programmable ROM is a AT49F040, a 4 megabit flash chip. This means the .ROM file to be programmed cannot be larger than 4 megabits, which excludes some of the larger ROMs out there. This circuit uses a salvaged Nintendo MBC (Memory Bank Con...",
      "displayName" : "Homebrew Gameboy Cartridge",
      "fullImage" : {
        "type" : "image/jpeg",
        "url" : "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kmgT78ODRdU/hqdefault.jpg"
      },
      "image" : {
        "height" : 910,
        "type" : "image/jpeg",
        "url" : "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/GYvc14qgigxKC77gtR0QkOlazZY5JV_rb9C2iPbMHSr0j2OQSdiLkNgZEeoGlRq6ZbfgeCj3QPFdnMcabrPbjA=w506-h910",
